OK   watchexec-cli rust-version lines in its published manifest (gate 2 FAIL) = 0
OK   bacon ships a run-long job that restarts on change (kill_then_restart)
OK   that job captures the child's stdout
OK   bacon's DEFAULT job interruption on unix is SIGKILL -- so a bacon.toml 'kill' override is required for a dev restart to run the production drain
OK   in --headless mode bacon prints the child's stdout/stderr straight to the terminal, not into a TUI pane
OK   bacon plumbs its --features flag into the cargo command
OK   arguments after -- are appended to the job's command tokens
OK   the -j argument is stored as settings.arg_job (src/conf/settings.rs)
OK   the initial job is settings.arg_job, falling back to default_job (src/jobs/job_stack.rs)
OK   references to 'headless' in bacon src/cli/mod.rs (all of them screen setup, none job selection) = 4
OK   headless only guards the alternate-screen setup around tui::app::run -- it does not touch job selection

